Advice (1)

  SURE    Index the referencing columns of order_items_order_id_fkey
          Each row deleted or updated makes PostgreSQL look up the rows that reference it through
          order_items_order_id_fkey. Without an index on the referencing columns, every lookup scans
          the referencing table.
          ! The plan does not say which columns order_items_order_id_fkey covers. This query names
          them: SELECT conrelid::regclass, pg_get_constraintdef(oid) FROM pg_constraint WHERE
          conname = 'order_items_order_id_fkey';
          ! Not connected to the database: existing indexes, the table's write load and the column
          statistics were not checked.

